  "prefLabel": "Env-A 3301.01 Purpose",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 3301.01 Purpose. The purpose of this chapter is to establish operating and performance standards for existing municipal waste combustion (MWC) units having the capacity to combust greater than 35 tons per day of municipal solid waste, in order to:\n\n(a) Comply with federal regulations promulgated pursuant to §111(d) and §129 of the Clean Air Act; and\n\n(b) Implement RSA 125-C:10-c relative to the combustion of processed wood residue.\n\nSource. #6518-B, eff 5-29-97; ss by #7704, eff 6-7-02; ss by #9084, eff 2-2-08; ss by #11131, eff 7-18-16; ss by #12628, eff 9-27-18",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a3300.html"
